---
title: "stdlib-semver"
author: bad-antics
date: 2026-04-07
abstract: Semantic Versioning 2.0.0 parsing, formatting, comparison, and range checks. A version is parsed into [major, minor, patch, prerelease, build], compared by precedence, and tested against caret and tilde ranges.

# Semantic Versioning

A version string has the form `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH`, optionally followed by a pre-release tag (`-...`) and build metadata (`+...`). The module parses this into a five-element list and provides accessors, comparison, and range helpers.

// Parse into components
parse("1.2.3")                  // [1, 2, 3, "", ""]
parse("1.2.3-beta.1+build.42")  // [1, 2, 3, "beta.1", "build.42"]

// A leading v is accepted and stripped
parse("v2.0.0")                 // [2, 0, 0, "", ""]

# Formatting

`format` builds the core `MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH` string; `format_full` appends pre-release and build metadata when present.

// Core formatting
format(1, 2, 3)                       // "1.2.3"

// Full formatting with pre-release and build
format_full(1, 2, 3, "beta.1", "b42") // "1.2.3-beta.1+b42"

# Accessors

The parsed list exposes its fields through helpers.

// Field access
major(parse("1.2.3"))       // 1
minor(parse("1.2.3"))       // 2
patch(parse("1.2.3"))       // 3
prerelease(parse("1.2.3"))  // ""
build_meta(parse("1.2.3"))  // ""

// Stability
is_stable(parse("1.2.3"))       // true
is_prerelease(parse("1.2.3-rc"))// true

# Comparison and Precedence

`compare` returns -1, 0, or 1 following semver.org precedence. A stable release has higher precedence than a pre-release of the same core version. Build metadata is ignored for precedence.

// Core precedence
compare(parse("1.0.0"), parse("2.0.0"))   // -1
compare(parse("2.0.0"), parse("2.0.0"))   // 0

// Pre-release ranks below the stable release
compare(parse("1.0.0-alpha"), parse("1.0.0"))  // -1

// Convenience predicates
lt(parse("1.0.0"), parse("1.0.1"))   // true
gte(parse("1.0.0"), parse("1.0.0"))  // true

# Bumping and Ranges

Version components can be incremented, and caret/tilde ranges checked.

// Increment the patch component
to_string(bump_patch(parse("1.2.3")))   // "1.2.4"

// Caret allows changes that do not modify the left-most non-zero digit
satisfies_caret(parse("1.2.3"), 1, 0)   // true
satisfies_caret(parse("2.0.0"), 1, 0)   // false

// Tilde allows patch-level changes within the same minor
satisfies_tilde(parse("1.2.9"), 1, 2)   // true
satisfies_tilde(parse("1.3.0"), 1, 2)   // false

# Canonical Vectors

Fixed vectors used across the test suite:

- parse("1.2.3") -> [1, 2, 3, "", ""]
- parse("v2.0.0") -> [2, 0, 0, "", ""]
- format(1, 2, 3) -> "1.2.3"
- compare("1.0.0", "2.0.0") -> -1
- compare("1.0.0-alpha", "1.0.0") -> -1
- is_stable("1.2.3") -> true
- to_string(bump_patch("1.2.3")) -> "1.2.4"

# Executable Program

fn main() {
    print(parse("1.2.3-beta.1+build.42"))
    print(compare(parse("1.0.0-alpha"), parse("1.0.0")))
    print(to_string(bump_patch(parse("1.2.3"))))
    print(satisfies_caret(parse("1.2.3"), 1, 0))
}

  </script>
  <script src="../ltlml.js"></script>
